			<item>
				<title>Tables</title>
				<link>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/tables/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/tables/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Hudocs 2.0 supports Markdown tables through Hugo&amp;rsquo;s built-in render hook. Tables use standard Markdown syntax and do not require custom shortcodes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;native-markdown-syntax&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Native Markdown Syntax&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Native Markdown Syntax&#39; href=&#34;#native-markdown-syntax&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Write tables using the standard GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM) syntax. The table is processed automatically when the site is built:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-markdown&#34; data-lang=&#34;markdown&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;| Column 1 | Column 2 | Column 3 |&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;| :------- | :------- | :------- |&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;| Row 1    | Value A  | Value B  |&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;| Row 2    | Value C  | Value D  |&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;horizontal-scrolling&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Horizontal Scrolling&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Horizontal Scrolling&#39; href=&#34;#horizontal-scrolling&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In Hudocs 2.0, each Markdown table is processed by the &lt;code&gt;render-table.html&lt;/code&gt; render hook, which adds the &lt;code&gt;.article-table&lt;/code&gt; container to allow horizontal scrolling when the table exceeds the available width:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Headings and Anchors</title>
				<link>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/headings-anchors/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/headings-anchors/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Hudocs generates anchor links for headings and an interactive Table of Contents (TOC) with active section tracking as you scroll.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;automatic-heading-anchors&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Automatic Heading Anchors&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Automatic Heading Anchors&#39; href=&#34;#automatic-heading-anchors&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Markdown headings are processed through Hugo&amp;rsquo;s custom render hook &lt;code&gt;render-heading.html&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;anchor-link&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Anchor Link&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Anchor Link&#39; href=&#34;#anchor-link&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When hovering over a heading, a &lt;code&gt;#&lt;/code&gt; symbol is displayed next to the text:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Clicking the symbol adds the heading identifier to the URL.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Users can copy and share direct links to specific sections of the document.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The link includes an &lt;code&gt;aria-label&lt;/code&gt; attribute to provide an accessible name for screen readers.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;table-of-contents-toc&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Table of Contents (TOC)&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Table of Contents (TOC)&#39; href=&#34;#table-of-contents-toc&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Each article automatically generates a Table of Contents in the right sidebar.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Badges and Icons</title>
				<link>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/badges-icons/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/badges-icons/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Hudocs allows you to add badges and icons to documentation pages to identify content and display additional information in the navigation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;status-badges&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Status Badges&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Status Badges&#39; href=&#34;#status-badges&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Badges appear next to links in the sidebar and next to the article&amp;rsquo;s main &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;h1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; title.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;enable-a-badge&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Enable a Badge&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Enable a Badge&#39; href=&#34;#enable-a-badge&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Add &lt;code&gt;badge: true&lt;/code&gt; to your article&amp;rsquo;s front matter:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-markdown&#34; data-lang=&#34;markdown&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nt&#34;&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;l&#34;&gt;Webhooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nt&#34;&gt;badge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kc&#34;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;By default, the badge displays the translated text &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;New&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Syntax Highlighting</title>
				<link>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/syntax-highlighting/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/syntax-highlighting/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Hudocs uses Hugo&amp;rsquo;s fenced code blocks to display code examples. In addition to syntax highlighting, these blocks let you customize their presentation using different options.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This page covers some of the most useful options. To see all available options, check the &lt;a href=&#34;https://gohugo.io/content-management/syntax-highlighting/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;official Hugo documentation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;file-name&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  File name&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: File name&#39; href=&#34;#file-name&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You can display the file name at the top of a code block using &lt;code&gt;filename&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34; filename=&#34;main.js&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-javascript&#34; data-lang=&#34;javascript&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kr&#34;&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;app&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;querySelector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s2&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;#app&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;app&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;textContent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;s2&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Hello, world!&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;line-numbers&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Line numbers&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Line numbers&#39; href=&#34;#line-numbers&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You can display numbers next to each line of code.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Images</title>
				<link>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/images/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://hudocs.com/docs/latest/markdown/images/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Hudocs optimizes images automatically using Hugo&amp;rsquo;s built-in image render hook (&lt;code&gt;render-image.html&lt;/code&gt;). Images use standard Markdown syntax and do not require custom shortcodes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;standard-syntax&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Standard Syntax&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Standard Syntax&#39; href=&#34;#standard-syntax&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Insert images using standard Markdown syntax:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-markdown&#34; data-lang=&#34;markdown&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;![&lt;span class=&#34;nt&#34;&gt;Architecture Diagram&lt;/span&gt;](&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;architecture.png &amp;#34;System Architecture&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;resource-resolution-and-dimensions&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Resource Resolution and Dimensions&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;article-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#39;Anchor: Resource Resolution and Dimensions&#39; href=&#34;#resource-resolution-and-dimensions&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When an image is processed, Hudocs looks for the image file in:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Page bundle resources:&lt;/strong&gt; files located alongside the page bundle (&lt;code&gt;.Page.Resources.GetMatch&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global asset resources:&lt;/strong&gt; files located inside &lt;code&gt;assets/&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;resources.Get&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When the image is found as a Hugo resource, its intrinsic dimensions (&lt;code&gt;width&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;height&lt;/code&gt;) are detected and injected into the rendered &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;img&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tag automatically. This prevents Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) as pages load.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
